) values
(t_econ,'both','mcq','Successive discounts of 20% and then 10% are equal to one single discount of:','30%','28%','32%','18%','b','The price becomes 0.8 x 0.9 = 0.72 of the original, a fall of 28%. Discounts never simply add.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A fair coin is tossed 4 times. What is the probability of exactly 2 heads?','1/4','1/2','3/8','5/8','c','There are 16 equally likely outcomes and 6 of them contain exactly two heads, giving 6/16 = 3/8.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','Half of a fixed distance is covered at 30 km/h and the other half at 60 km/h. The average speed is:','50 km/h','45 km/h','48 km/h','40 km/h','d','Average speed is total distance over total time. More time is spent on the slow half, so the answer sits below 45: it is 40 km/h.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','Umbrella sales rise when traffic slows, so umbrellas cause traffic jams. What is the best challenge to this?','Rain could be causing both','Umbrellas are small','Traffic never changes','Sales data cannot be numeric','a','A third factor explains both at once. Rain drives up umbrella sales AND slows traffic, so neither causes the other.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A 3-digit code uses different digits chosen from 1, 2, 3, 4, and the first digit must be even. How many codes are possible?','8','12','10','16','b','The first digit is 2 or 4 (2 ways). The remaining two positions take any 2 of the 3 unused digits in order: 3 x 2 = 6. Total 2 x 6 = 12.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','What is the best evidence that a new study method improves results?','Ask students who liked it','Compare the two top students','Compare a group using it with a similar control group','Ask if scores felt higher','c','Only a comparison against a similar group that did NOT use the method separates the method''s effect from everything else.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','Two fair dice are rolled. The probability that the total is 7 is:','1/12','5/36','1/8','1/6','d','Six of the 36 equally likely pairs total seven, so 6/36 = 1/6. Seven is the most likely total.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A jar holds 5 red and 5 blue balls. Two are drawn without replacement. The probability both are red is:','2/9','1/4','1/5','5/18','a','The first is red with probability 5/10. With one red gone, the second is red with probability 4/9. Multiplying gives 20/90 = 2/9.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_econ,'both','mcq','1000 rupees is invested at 10% compound interest for 2 years. The amount is:','1100','1210','1200','1220','b','Year one adds 100 to make 1100; year two adds 10% of 1100, which is 110. The total is 1210.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_econ,'both','mcq','On 1000 rupees at 10% for 2 years, by how much does compound interest exceed simple interest?','0','20','10','100','c','Simple interest gives 200; compound gives 210. The 10-rupee gap is the interest earned on the first year''s interest.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A class averages 60 marks. One more student scoring 80 raises the average to 61. How many students were there BEFORE?','15','21','20','19','d','If n students averaged 60, then (60n + 80)/(n+1) = 61. Solving gives 60n + 80 = 61n + 61, so n = 19.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','To learn how many people in a town have internet access, a researcher surveys people through a smartphone app. The main flaw is:','Everyone surveyed is already online','The sample is too small','Phones give wrong answers','The question is unclear','a','The method can only reach people who already have access, so it cannot possibly find those who do not. That is sampling bias.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','Ice cream sales and drowning deaths rise and fall together across the year. The most likely explanation is:','Ice cream causes drowning','Hot weather raises both','Drowning causes ice cream sales','Pure coincidence with no cause','b','Warm weather independently drives both swimming and ice cream buying. It is a confounding variable, not a link between the two.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','"If it rained, the ground is wet." The ground is NOT wet. What follows?','It rained','It may have rained','It did not rain','Nothing follows','c','If the consequence is false the condition must be false too. This is valid reasoning.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','"If it rained, the ground is wet." The ground IS wet. What follows about rain?','It definitely rained','It definitely did not rain','It rained heavily','Nothing certain - something else could have wet it','d','A sprinkler or a burst pipe would also do it. Concluding rain from a wet ground is the classic invalid step.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A disease affects 1 person in 10,000. A test is 99% accurate. Someone tests positive. Most likely, that person:','Probably does NOT have the disease','Probably has the disease','Definitely has the disease','Cannot be assessed at all','a','In a million people about 100 have it, but 1% of the other 999,900 - nearly 10,000 people - test positive wrongly. A positive result is far more often a false alarm.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_econ,'both','mcq','A car worth 100,000 rupees loses 20% of its value each year. After 2 years it is worth:','60,000','64,000','68,000','80,000','b','Each year multiplies by 0.8: 100,000 x 0.8 x 0.8 = 64,000. Subtracting 40% outright gives the trap 60,000.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','Which is the stronger evidence that a medicine works?','A letter from a satisfied patient','A famous person endorsing it','A trial where patients were randomly given the medicine or a dummy','The manufacturer''s own claim','c','Random allocation and a comparison group remove the alternative explanations that a single story cannot rule out.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A study finds students who eat breakfast score higher. Its main weakness is that it:','Used too many students','Should have used older students','Measured scores incorrectly','Cannot show breakfast CAUSED the higher scores','d','Households where breakfast happens may differ in many other ways. Observing a pattern does not establish which way the cause runs.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','With 3 shirts and 4 pairs of trousers, how many different outfits are possible?','12','7','14','24','a','Every shirt can pair with every pair of trousers: 3 x 4 = 12.','medium','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','In how many different orders can the four letters of TEAM be arranged?','12','24','16','48','b','Four choices, then three, then two, then one: 4 x 3 x 2 x 1 = 24. All four letters differ.','medium','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','One card is drawn from a standard 52-card pack. The probability it is an ace is:','1/4','1/26','1/13','4/13','c','There are 4 aces among 52 cards: 4/52 = 1/13.','medium','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','Two independent events have probabilities 0.5 and 0.4. The probability both happen is:','0.1','0.9','0.45','0.2','d','For independent events the probabilities multiply: 0.5 x 0.4 = 0.2.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_econ,'both','mcq','After a 20% discount a shirt costs 500 rupees. Its original price was:','625','600','575','650','a','500 is 80% of the original, so the original is 500/0.8 = 625. Adding 20% back gives the trap 600.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A 10 m ladder rests against a wall with its base 6 m out. How high up the wall does it reach?','7 m','8 m','9 m','12 m','b','The wall, ground and ladder form a right-angled triangle: 10 squared minus 6 squared is 64, whose square root is 8.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','The sum of the first 50 whole numbers (1 to 50) is:','1225','1250','1275','2550','c','Pair them: 1+50, 2+49 and so on gives 25 pairs of 51, which is 1275.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A cyclist rides the first third of a journey at 10 km/h and the remaining two thirds at 20 km/h. The average speed is:','13.3 km/h','18 km/h','16.7 km/h','15 km/h','d','Take the trip as 3 km. The first km takes 0.1 h and the next two take 0.1 h - 3 km in 0.2 h, which is 15 km/h.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','An advertisement states "80% of doctors recommend this brand". What matters MOST before believing it?','How many doctors were asked and who paid for the survey','The brand''s colour','Whether it rhymes','How long the brand has existed','a','A percentage without its sample size or its funding source can be produced from a handful of hand-picked people.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A fair coin is tossed 3 times. The probability of AT LEAST one head is:','1/2','7/8','3/4','5/8','b','The only excluded outcome is three tails, which has probability 1/8. So the answer is 1 - 1/8 = 7/8.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','In a town 40% read paper A, 30% read paper B and 10% read both. What percentage reads at least one?','50%','70%','60%','80%','c','Adding 40 and 30 counts the overlap twice, so subtract it once: 40 + 30 - 10 = 60.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A rectangle''s length is doubled and its width is halved. Its area is:','Doubled','Halved','Four times larger','Unchanged','d','Area is length times width, and the factors 2 and 1/2 cancel exactly. The perimeter does change.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sport,'both','mcq','Six teams each play every other team once. How many matches are played in total?','15','12','30','36','a','Each of six teams plays five others, giving 30 - but each match is counted from both sides, so 30/2 = 15.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','To gauge the whole school''s opinion, the most representative sample is:','The first 30 students to arrive','30 students chosen at random from every class','30 volunteers','The 30 students with the best marks','b','Random selection across all classes gives every student a comparable chance of being chosen. The other three each select a particular kind of student.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_sci,'both','mcq','A water tank loses 5% of its remaining water each day. After 2 days, roughly what fraction is left?','85%','90%','90.25%','95%','c','Each day multiplies by 0.95: 0.95 x 0.95 = 0.9025, which is 90.25%.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false),
(t_young,'both','mcq','A project claims it "helped over 1,000 young people". Which single detail would tell you the most about whether it worked?','The number reached','The number of photographs taken','The size of the launch event','What changed for them, measured before and after','d','Reach counts people touched, not outcomes. Only a before-and-after measure shows whether anything actually changed.','hard','YIQ Reasoning Bank 2026 - THE FINAL CHALLENGE','practice',true,null,true,false);

